           cells at 120 px a cell, the airframe 33.5 x 26.7 of it (C27J.layout.json; assets/phobos-vehicles/export_c27j.py). -->
      <drawSize>(34, 27)</drawSize>
      <!-- The pick's own grey, measured by the export (C27J.transform.json). It has no second colour (no band or stripe), so the paint
           masks are main paint only and colorTwo paints nothing; it repeats the main grey. -->
      <color>(225, 224, 234)</color>
      <colorTwo>(225, 224, 234)</colorTwo>
    </graphicData>
    <fillPercent>1</fillPercent>
    <buildDef>Phobos_C27J_Blueprint</buildDef>
    <size>(5, 11)</size>
    <vehicleCategory>Transport</vehicleCategory>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <vehicleType>Air</vehicleType>
    <statBases>
      <!-- Read only for collisions: every part carries its own armour by class, which overrides these (vehicle-armour.md). Heat stays the
           whole aircraft's. -->
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.1</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1.0</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Flammability>0.8</Flammability>
      <!-- 15,000 [A]: below the Osprey's 18,000, as the real aircraft costs well under a V-22. -->
      <MarketValue>15000</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <vehicleStats>
      <!-- 2,200: the Osprey's 1,950 for 15,032 kg empty, scaled to the C-27J's 17,000 kg [P4] [I]. -->
      <Mass>2200</Mass>
      <!-- 22: the Osprey's 17.5 for 463 to 493 km/h, scaled to the C-27J's 602 km/h cruise [P1] [I]. -->
      <FlightSpeed>22</FlightSpeed>
      <!-- Taxiing on its wheels [A], as the Osprey. -->
      <MoveSpeed>4</MoveSpeed>
      <!-- Real kilograms: its 11,300 kg maximum payload [P1, P4]. The owner's hold (8,600 kg, one vehicle) fits within it. Our flight's
           take-off check holds it to its 32,500 kg maximum take-off weight [P1, P4] with what is aboard: with full fuel (9,734 kg) it lifts
           5,766 kg; more payload needs less fuel, as the real aircraft trades them [I]. -->
      <CargoCapacity>11300</CargoCapacity>
      <RepairRate>0.4</RepairRate>
      <AccelerationRate>0.03</AccelerationRate>
    </vehicleStats>
